#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/manjaro-linux.md:0
msgid ""
"Learn how to install or restore snap on Manjaro through Pamac or the command "
"line, enable the socket and classic support, and test with hello-world."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/manjaro-linux.md:8
msgid "Install snap on Manjaro Linux"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/manjaro-linux.md:10
msgid ""
"Snap is often installed by default on Manjaro, especially if you're using a "
"KDE Plasma desktop. If not, or if it's been removed,  it can easily be  "
"installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/manjaro-linux.md:12
msgid ""
"The easiest way to install Snap is from Manjaro's *Add/Remove Software* "
"application (Pamac), found in the launch menu. From the application, search "
"for `snapd`, select the result, and click *Apply*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/manjaro-linux.md:14
msgid ""
"An optional dependency is *bash completion support*, which we recommend "
"leaving enabled when prompted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/manjaro-linux.md:16
msgid "Alternatively, *snapd* can be installed from the command line:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/manjaro-linux.md:18
msgid "sudo pacman -S snapd\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/manjaro-linux.md:22
msgid ""
"Once installed, the *systemd* unit that manages the main snap communication "
"socket needs to be enabled:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/manjaro-linux.md:24
msgid "sudo systemctl enable --now snapd.socket\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/manjaro-linux.md:28
msgid ""
"To enable *classic* snap support, enter the following to create a symbolic "
"link between `/var/lib/snapd/snap` and `/snap`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/manjaro-linux.md:30
msgid "sudo ln -s /var/lib/snapd/snap /snap\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/manjaro-linux.md:34
msgid ""
"Restart your system to ensure snap’s paths and AppArmor are initialised and "
"updated correctly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/manjaro-linux.md:36
msgid ""
"To test your system, install the [hello-world](https://snapcraft.io/hello-"
"world) snap and make sure it runs correctly:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/manjaro-linux.md:38
msgid ""
"$ sudo snap install hello-world\n"
"hello-world 6.3 from Canonical✓ installed\n"
"$ hello-world\n"
"Hello World!\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/manjaro-linux.md:45
msgid "Snap is now installed and ready to go!"
msgstr ""
